WEBVTT

NOTE week12-clip1-trial
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.083 line:2 align:center
A benchmark asks whether
the model can answer.

2
00:00:03.083 --> 00:00:08.389 line:2 align:center
A trial asks whether clinicians do better
with it. These are different questions,

3
00:00:08.389 --> 00:00:13.350 line:2 align:center
and only the second one decides
whether a tool helps patients.

4
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.973 line:2 align:center
Goh and colleagues
randomized 50 physicians:

5
00:00:16.973 --> 00:00:24.817 line:2 align:center
25 to GPT-4 plus their usual resources,
and 25 to usual resources alone.

6
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:29.185 line:2 align:center
Both groups worked up to
6 vignettes in 60 minutes,

7
00:00:29.185 --> 00:00:33.417 line:2 align:center
graded blind on a structured
reflection rubric.

8
00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:36.683 line:2 align:center
The median diagnostic reasoning score per

9
00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:41.697 line:2 align:center
case was 76% with GPT-4 and 74% without.

10
00:00:41.697 --> 00:00:45.063 line:2 align:center
The adjusted difference was 2%age points,

11
00:00:45.063 --> 00:00:51.085 line:2 align:center
with a 95% interval from minus
4 to 8 and a P value of 0.60.

12
00:00:51.085 --> 00:00:54.083 line:2 align:center
The interval includes zero.

13
00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:55.918 line:2 align:center
Nor was it faster.

14
00:00:55.918 --> 00:01:01.871 line:2 align:center
Physicians with the model took
519 seconds per case against 565,

15
00:01:01.871 --> 00:01:04.879 line:2 align:center
a difference of minus 82 seconds,

16
00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:09.801 line:2 align:center
with a 95% interval from minus 195 to 31.

17
00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:13.083 line:2 align:center
That interval includes zero too.

18
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:20.161 line:2 align:center
In an exploratory arm of 3 runs, the
model alone scored a median of 92%,

19
00:01:20.161 --> 00:01:22.513 line:2 align:center
16 points above the control group.

20
00:01:22.513 --> 00:01:26.867 line:2 align:center
But the physicians who had
that same model scored 76.

21
00:01:26.867 --> 00:01:31.883 line:2 align:center
The gap is about how people use
the tool, not about the tool.

22
00:01:32.083 --> 00:01:37.539 line:2 align:center
Benchmark, retrospective study,
reader study, prospective trial,

23
00:01:37.539 --> 00:01:39.569 line:2 align:center
then deployment with monitoring.

24
00:01:39.569 --> 00:01:45.989 line:2 align:center
Each rung answers a question the one below
it cannot. This trial is the fourth rung,

25
00:01:45.989 --> 00:01:50.213 line:2 align:center
and most published
results stop at the first.
